 "architecture": {
  "summary": "sharingu is Agent R (QA78C4808) — engine/ is the whole product: a served console + a REST/MCP door (107 REST routes · 47 MCP tools, contracts/door.json), one Cloudflare Worker per org with its own D1 (15 tables, 38 migrations), R2 brain bucket and KV (M-ADR-094/013/027: org = hard-walled worker, project = soft scope inside it). ONE org worker is deployed today — ryuklabs-agent-r (engine/wrangler.jsonc; QC74D4892) — with its projects inside it as data; a new org gets its own worker from engine/wrangler.tenant.template.jsonc (tools/new-org.sh). There is no L agent: orchestrator/ is this repo's own native agentic SDLC (the crew files in .claude/agents/, the lane workflow, the land door, the gates, the run record), used only to build sharingu (QF281329F) — no org, user or stranger needs it, and no manifest is sent to orgs. It reaches R through one seam: contracts/door.json, GENERATED from R's own registries by engine/tools/make-door-contract.py — read, never R's source. GitHub (ryukdev/sharingu) hosts both lanes; CI is LOCAL (Q02FA9104): the land door runs the gates on the exact sha.",
  "diagram": {
   "width": 680,
   "height": 420,
   "groups": [
    {
     "id": "cloudflare",
     "label": "Cloudflare — one Worker per org (deployed today: ryuklabs-agent-r)",
     "x": 30,
     "y": 30,
     "w": 620,
     "h": 160,
     "labelX": 46,
     "labelY": 46
    },
    {
     "id": "machine",
     "label": "This repo's own build machine — the native SDLC, builds sharingu only (QA78C4808)",
     "x": 30,
     "y": 220,
     "w": 620,
     "h": 160,
     "labelX": 46,
     "labelY": 236
    }
   ],
   "nodes": [
    {
     "id": "browser",
     "kind": "client",
     "title": "Browser / Claude Code (MCP)",
     "sub": "a reader on glass, or an MCP client",
     "x": 50,
     "y": 60,
     "w": 200,
     "h": 50
    },
    {
     "id": "worker",
     "kind": "worker",
